            <ArticleTitle>MONOSTOTIC PAGET'S DISEASE IN LUMBAR VERTEBRAE: AN ATYPICAL LOCATION.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>200-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/S2255-4971(15)30294-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 41-year-old white female patient with complaints of lumbar pain for more than three years, without irradiation, underwent several radiological examinations. Her condition was diagnosed by means of biopsy, as monostotic Paget' s disease in the third lumbar vertebra. This is an uncommon location.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
